+#### Keep Localization for a Single-Language App
+
+Localization is a load-bearing module: routing, shared widgets and feature
+screens use `AppLocalizations` even when the app offers only one language.
+Keep `lib/core/localization`, `lib/l10n`, the app's localization delegates and
+supported-locale configuration, and the `flutter_localizations` and `intl`
+dependencies. Deleting those pieces alone leaves their consumers uncompilable.
+
+For a single-language app, keep one locale instead of removing the localization
+API. Treat narrowing the language set as a coordinated customization:
+`SupportedLocale` in `lib/core/localization/localization_service.dart`, its
+fallback, the ARB files and `l10n.yaml` must agree. Regenerate the committed
+localizations with `flutter gen-l10n`, retaining the UI delegate adapters in the
+`l10n.yaml` header. Update language-picker and locale-specific tests for the
+chosen language, and run `test/core/localization/supported_locales_test.dart`
+plus `flutter analyze` and the full test suite. See the
+[internationalization guide](../features/internationalization-guide.md) for the
+localization setup and generation process. This keeps existing translated-string
+calls working without a rewrite of every screen and shared consumer.
+
+#### Keep Secure Storage Until Its Consumers Are Migrated
+
+Secure storage is also load-bearing in the default app. Keep
+`secure_storage_service.dart`, `secureStorageServiceProvider` and
+`flutter_secure_storage` while core DI, `ApiClient`, `AuthInterceptor`,
+`SecureTokenStore` and `StorageMigrationService` still depend on the service.
+Removing just the file, provider and package breaks these consumers.
+
+If your app uses another credential vault, provide an `ITokenStore` adapter at
+the composition root and preserve its mutation ordering, certified snapshots
+and failure/clear semantics. An adapter override alone does not remove the
+remaining concrete-service imports or the storage migration path: migrate those
+consumers deliberately before deleting the default implementation or package.
+Do not replace credential storage with ordinary preferences to make the build
+pass. See the [storage contracts and replacement requirements](../../api/core/storage.md)
+and [storage migration guide](../features/storage-migration-guide.md), then run
+`flutter analyze` and the auth, network and storage tests after customization.
 
